{"entries":[{"id":"tsk-exo-1-intro","title":"Exodus 1 — Chapter Introduction","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"EXO","chapterStart":1,"verseStart":0,"chapterEnd":1,"verseEnd":0},"content":"<p>had made. 1,24-26; Jos 24:27-29; Heb 11:22 and yielded. 29; 15:5; 25:8,17; 35:29; Job 5:26; 14:10; 30:23; Ec 12:7; Isa 57:1,2 Lu 2:29; Heb 11:13-16; 12:23</p>"},{"id":"tsk-exo-1-1","title":"Exodus 1:1","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"EXO","chapterStart":1,"verseStart":1,"chapterEnd":1,"verseEnd":1},"content":"<p>The title of this Book is derived from the Septuagint; in which it is called [exodos,], \"Exodus;\" or, as it is in the Codex Alexandrinus, [exodos aiguptou,] \"the Exodus or departure from Egypt;\" but it is called in Hebrew Bibles [w'lh shmwt,] {Weelleh Shemoth,} \"these are the names\", or merely, [shmwt,] {Shemoth,} \"names\", from the words with which it commences. 1 The children of Israel, after Joseph's death, increase. 8 The more they are oppressed by a new king, the more they multiply. 15 The godliness of the midwives, in saving the men children alive. 22 Pharaoh commands the male children to be cast into the river. 6:14-16; Ge 29:31-35; 30:1-21; 35:18,23-26; 46:8-26; 49:3-27 1Ch 2:1,2; 12:23-40; 27:16-22; Re 7:4-8</p>"},{"id":"tsk-exo-1-2","title":"Exodus 1:2","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"EXO","chapterStart":1,"verseStart":2,"chapterEnd":1,"verseEnd":2},"content":"<p>Reuben. Ge 35:22</p>"},{"id":"tsk-exo-1-3","title":"Exodus 1:3","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"EXO","chapterStart":1,"verseStart":3,"chapterEnd":1,"verseEnd":3},"content":"<p>Issachar. Ge 35:23 Benjamin. 28:20</p>"},{"id":"tsk-exo-1-5","title":"Exodus 1:5","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"EXO","chapterStart":1,"verseStart":5,"chapterEnd":1,"verseEnd":5},"content":"<p>loins. Heb. thigh. Ge 46:26; Jud 8:30; *marg: seventy. 20; Ge 46:26,27; De 10:22</p>"},{"id":"tsk-exo-1-6","title":"Exodus 1:6","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"EXO","chapterStart":1,"verseStart":6,"chapterEnd":1,"verseEnd":6},"content":"<p>A.M. 2369. B.C. 1635. Ge 50:24,26; Ac 7:14-16</p>"},{"id":"tsk-exo-1-7","title":"Exodus 1:7","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"EXO","chapterStart":1,"verseStart":7,"chapterEnd":1,"verseEnd":7},"content":"<p>fruitful. 12:37; Ge 1:20,28; 9:1; 12:2; 13:16; 15:5; 17:4-6,16; 22:17; 26:4 Ge 28:3,4,14; 35:11; 46:3; 47:27; 48:4,16; De 10:22; 26:5; Ne 9:23 Ps 105:24; Ac 7:17,18</p>"},{"id":"tsk-exo-1-8","title":"Exodus 1:8","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"EXO","chapterStart":1,"verseStart":8,"chapterEnd":1,"verseEnd":8},"content":"<p>a new king.Probably Rameses Miamum, or his son Amenophis, who succeeded him about this period; and by his not knowing Joseph is meant his not acknowledging his obligation to him.</p>\n<p>Ec 2:18,19; 9:15; Ac 7:18</p>"},{"id":"tsk-exo-1-9","title":"Exodus 1:9","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"EXO","chapterStart":1,"verseStart":9,"chapterEnd":1,"verseEnd":9},"content":"<p>the people. Nu 22:4,5; Job 5:2; Ps 105:24,25; Pr 14:28; 27:4; Ec 4:4; Tit 3:3 Jas 3:14-16; 4:5</p>"},{"id":"tsk-exo-1-10","title":"Exodus 1:10","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"EXO","chapterStart":1,"verseStart":10,"chapterEnd":1,"verseEnd":10},"content":"<p>Come on. Ps 10:2; 83:3,4; Pr 1:11 wisely. Nu 22:6; Job 5:13; Ps 105:25; Pr 16:25; 21:30; Ac 7:19; 23:12 1Co 3:18-20; Jas 3:15-18</p>"},{"id":"tsk-exo-1-11","title":"Exodus 1:11","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"EXO","chapterStart":1,"verseStart":11,"chapterEnd":1,"verseEnd":11},"content":"<p>to afflict. 3:7; 5:15; Ge 15:13; Nu 20:15; De 26:6 burdens. 2:11; 5:4,5; Ps 68:13; 81:6; 105:13 Raamses. Ge 47:11; Pr 27:4</p>"},{"id":"tsk-exo-1-12","title":"Exodus 1:12","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"EXO","chapterStart":1,"verseStart":12,"chapterEnd":1,"verseEnd":12},"content":"<p>But the more, etc. Heb. and as they afflicted them, so theymultiplied, etc. Ps 105:24; Pr 21:30; Ro 8:28; Heb 12:6-11 grieved. 9; Job 5:2; Pr 27:4; Joh 12:19; Ac 4:2-4; 5:28-33</p>"},{"id":"tsk-exo-1-14","title":"Exodus 1:14","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"EXO","chapterStart":1,"verseStart":14,"chapterEnd":1,"verseEnd":14},"content":"<p>their lives. 2:23; 6:9; Ge 15:13; Nu 20:15; De 4:20; 26:6; Ru 1:20; Ac 7:19,34 in mortar. Ps 68:13; 81:6; Na 3:14 was with rigour. 13; 5:7-21; 20:2; Le 25:43,46,53; Isa 14:6; 51:23; 52:5; 58:6 Jer 50:33,34; Mic 3:3</p>"},{"id":"tsk-exo-1-16","title":"Exodus 1:16","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"EXO","chapterStart":1,"verseStart":16,"chapterEnd":1,"verseEnd":16},"content":"<p>and see them.Or, rather, \"and ye see them by the stone-troughs;\" for so {ovnayim,} from {aven,} a stone, seems to signify (compare ch. 7:19), in which they washed the new-born infants. See this subject fully illustrated in Fragments to Calmet, Nos. 312, 313.</p>\n<p>then ye shall. 22; Mt 21:38; Re 12:4</p>"},{"id":"tsk-exo-1-17","title":"Exodus 1:17","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"EXO","chapterStart":1,"verseStart":17,"chapterEnd":1,"verseEnd":17},"content":"<p>feared God. Ge 20:11; 42:18; Ne 5:15; Ps 31:19; Pr 8:13; 16:6; 24:11,12; Ec 8:12 Ec 12:13; Da 3:16-18; 6:13; Ho 5:11; Mic 6:16; Mt 10:28; Lu 12:5 Ac 4:19; 5:29</p>"},{"id":"tsk-exo-1-18","title":"Exodus 1:18","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"EXO","chapterStart":1,"verseStart":18,"chapterEnd":1,"verseEnd":18},"content":"<p>Why have. 2Sa 13:28; Ec 8:4</p>"},{"id":"tsk-exo-1-19","title":"Exodus 1:19","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"EXO","chapterStart":1,"verseStart":19,"chapterEnd":1,"verseEnd":19},"content":"<p>Jos 2:4-24; 1Sa 21:2; 2Sa 17:19,20</p>"},{"id":"tsk-exo-1-20","title":"Exodus 1:20","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"EXO","chapterStart":1,"verseStart":20,"chapterEnd":1,"verseEnd":20},"content":"<p>God. Ps 41:1,2; 61:5; 85:9; 103:11; 111:5; 145:19; Pr 11:18; 19:17 Ec 8:12; Isa 3:10; Mt 10:42; 25:40; Lu 1:50; Heb 6:10 the people. 7,12</p>"},{"id":"tsk-exo-1-21","title":"Exodus 1:21","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"EXO","chapterStart":1,"verseStart":21,"chapterEnd":1,"verseEnd":21},"content":"<p>made them. 1Sa 2:35; 25:28; 2Sa 7:11-13,27-29; 1Ki 2:24; 11:38; Ps 37:3 Ps 127:1,3; Pr 24:3; Ec 8:12; Jer 35:2</p>"},{"id":"tsk-exo-1-22","title":"Exodus 1:22","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"EXO","chapterStart":1,"verseStart":22,"chapterEnd":1,"verseEnd":22},"content":"<p>A.M. 2431. B.C. 1573. Every son. 16; 7:19-21; Ps 105:25; Pr 1:16; 4:16; 27:4; Ac 7:19; Re 16:4-6</p>"}]}